    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nReplaced the direct level computation with a two-stage **points \u2192 level** system.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the old `membershipLevel(Owner)` with:\n- `membershipPoints(Owner)`: starts at 0; **+2** email present, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), **+3** tenure > 365 days since `registrationDate`.\n- `membershipLevel(Owner)`: bands the points \u2192 **1** (0\u20131), **2** (2\u20133), **3** (4\u20135), **4** (6+).\n- Added a `@Mapping` so `OwnerDto.membershipPoints` is populated alongside `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it) and updated the `membershipLevel` schema (now 1\u20134, banded description).\n\n`AuditOwnerCreated` still calls `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)`, which remains valid.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe lone `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 **3 points, level 2** \u2014 passes:\n\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\n(The audit log line confirms `membershipLevel=2` for that created owner.)\n\nNote: the previous rule ignored `householdSize` entirely; the new points system uses it (+2 for households of 3+), which is now the only factor that can lift a *newly created* owner toward the higher bands before tenure accrues.",
