    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the complete ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`owners.POST.yml` `composition.authorize`). No role \u2192 rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\nThe pipeline then runs these steps in order. Every step **except `validate`** runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all DB reads/writes share one transaction that commits once at the very end.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 validation + normalization of the body\nReads `@RequestBody` (the only step that binds the body; it republishes it as a variable). In order:\n1. **Normalize address** (`OwnerAddress.normalize`): trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Null/blank \u2192 `\"\"`. Written back onto the request.\n2. **Required-field check**: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (after normalization), `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**), collected as a list.\n3. **Normalize telephone to E.164** (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep a leading `+`, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; must be `+` and 8\u201315 digits; for `+61` national part must be 9 digits, for `+1` must be 10. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**). Written back.\n4. **Normalize email** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`), only if present: syntactic check \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**); lower-cased; domain against a disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (**400**). Blank/null \u2192 stored as null. Written back.\n5. **Normalize/validate postcode** (`Postcode.normalize`), only if present: must be 4 digits \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**); if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 **400**. Trimmed value written back.\n\n## 2. `EnsureIdentityUnique` \u2014 hard duplicate check (409)\nSkipped if the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`. Otherwise derives a household id from normalized lastName + postcode and scans **all existing owners**; if any existing owner has the same household id \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n## 3. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2014 city capacity check (409)\nCounts existing owners whose city matches (trim + case-insensitive). If count \u2265 `CAPACITY` (50) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**). New owner not yet counted.\n\n## 4. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` \u2014 daily limit check (429)\nComputes the effective registration date (request value, or today if null) rolled forward off weekends to the next Monday. Counts existing owners already on that business day; if \u2265 `LIMIT` (100) \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct the entity (+ future-date validation)\nMaps the DTO to an `Owner` via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`. Effective registration date defaults to today if null; if a supplied date is **after** today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). The registration date is then rolled forward off weekends to the next Monday and stored on the entity.\n\n## 6. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION from postcode (NSW/VIC/QLD else `UNKNOWN`), HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## 7. `AssignHouseholdId` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `householdId` (first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized lastName + postcode) and `householdSize` (existing members sharing that id, plus this owner).\n\n## 8. `CountNamesakes` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners whose firstName and lastName both match (case-insensitive); unique name \u2192 0.\n\n## 9. `FlagBulkSignup` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `bulkSignupWarning=true` if more than `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD` (80) existing owners already share this owner's stored business day; else false.\n\n## 10. `FlagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 side-effect\nInitializes `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Skipped (left unflagged) if `sharesHousehold=true` or postcode is blank. Otherwise, if an existing owner shares normalized lastName + postcode but has a **different** canonical telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the lowest matching id. The owner is still created.\n\n## 11. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect (persist)\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the write that assigns the id. (All prior \"count existing owners\" steps therefore excluded this new owner.)\n\n## 12. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (audit log)\nEmits an `AUDIT` logger line with the saved owner's id, customerCode, registrationDate, and computed membershipLevel. Runs after save so the id exists.\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response\nMaps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes on ordering rationale\n- Validation deliberately precedes the load/existence checks so a bad body is a 400 rather than being masked.\n- The three limit/uniqueness gates (2\u20134) run before `BuildOwner` and `SaveOwner`, so they count only pre-existing owners.\n- Because governance spans steps 2\u201313, a failure anywhere rolls the whole request back; success commits once after `respond`.\n\nAny unmatched escalation falls through to Spring's `@RestControllerAdvice`."
